    "question": "Find the minimum positive integer x such that 1 ≤ x ≤ 50 satisfying both:\n- x ≡ 1 (mod 3)\n- x ≡ 2 (mod 5)",
    "rationale": "We seek the smallest x in [1,50] where x≡1(mod 3) and x≡2(mod 5). By Chinese Remainder Theorem, since gcd(3,5)=1, there is a unique solution mod 15. Checking values: 1≡1(mod 3) but 1≠2(mod 5); 4≡1(mod 3) but 4≠2(mod 5); 7≡1(mod 3) and 7≡2(mod 5). Thus 7 is the minimum. The verifier confirms this answer.",
    "rubric": [
      {
        "criterion": "correct_constraints",
        "description": "Problem specifies two modular constraints with coprime moduli"
      },
      {
        "criterion": "unique_answer",
        "description": "Answer is uniquely determined by the constraints"
      }
    ],
